# RoamWise -- environment template (issue #7)
#
# Copy to .env, fill in your OWN key, and load it into the shell you are
# running the app from:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   $EDITOR .env
#   set -a; source .env; set +a
#   cd roamwise && streamlit run app.py
#
# .env is gitignored; this file is not. The repository is public: a key
# committed once must be REVOKED, not deleted -- rewriting history does not
# un-publish it. Each team member uses their own key and their own quota, so
# nobody's calls land on someone else's limit.
#
# Load this per shell rather than from .zshrc: ROAMWISE_LLM is what authorises
# spending, and a shell profile would hand it to every later pytest run and
# evaluation script too.

# Which narration engine to use: nvidia | anthropic | local | template
# Unset means the offline template, which needs no key and cannot cost
# anything. Leave it unset in any deployed container.
ROAMWISE_LLM=nvidia

# Your own key from build.nvidia.com.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# --- everything below is optional ---

# The model. Defaults to the value shown; set it to anything your account can
# reach. If the model is not available to your key the endpoint answers 404,
# and the app says so rather than failing quietly.
# NVIDIA_LLM_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b

# Reasoning models deliberate before answering and return that deliberation
# separately. RoamWise wants the narration, not the deliberation -- nothing
# reads it, and it is billed like any other output token -- so thinking is
# sent as disabled. Set this to 1 only for a model that needs it.
# ROAMWISE_LLM_THINKING=0

# Requests per minute this process allows itself, matching NVIDIA's free tier.
# One plan costs two generations, so 40/min is twenty plans a minute. Set 0 to
# disable the limiter on a paid tier.
# ROAMWISE_LLM_RPM=40

# Point the same client at another OpenAI-compatible gateway.
# NVIDIA_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
